  "id": "COMPOUND:35932 - PROTEIN:5852",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Caryolan-1-ol is implicated in the biological activity of BT-474 through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately target the cancer cell. The evidence suggests that (+)-Caryolan-1-ol acts as a target for hepatocytes and for SNB-78, which in turn is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is shared as a target among multiple entities, indicating a potential common mechanism of action. The presence of multiple pathways converging on BT-474 suggests that (+)-Caryolan-1-ol may exert its effects through a shared molecular interaction, possibly involving the activation of downstream signaling pathways in BT-474 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One as a central mediator in the relationship between (+)-Caryolan-1-ol and BT-474, reinforcing the hypothesis that the drug's activity is linked to the modulation of this specific compound.",
